From: ThaRae <76752281+ThaRae@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:35:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Tests/LibWeb: Wheel over an isolated iframe once it has drawn

The iframe's document said it was ready from a script in its head,
before it had a body to scroll or had drawn a frame. The wheel reaches
that document through its parent's process and the UI, and the
compositor scrolls for the step the document lets through only if its
last frame of the iframe is of that document. When the iframe's process
took the wheel before its first rendering update, the compositor had no
frame of the document yet, answered that the scroller was in another
document, and nothing scrolled. The test then waited for a scroll event
that never came, and timed out now and then on slow runners.

Say ready after two frames and a synchronization of the compositor, as
the other tests that send input to an isolated iframe do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../iframe/wheel-scrolls-an-isolated-iframe.html             | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Tests/LibWeb/Text/input/SiteIsolation/iframe/wheel-scrolls-an-isolated-iframe.html b/Tests/LibWeb/Text/input/SiteIsolation/iframe/wheel-scrolls-an-isolated-iframe.html
index b503ccf59cd28f32fd11d31fa4f281bf26d481d5..49ba843d98d68177d66e76dab52aea56a1209ca7 100644
--- a/Tests/LibWeb/Text/input/SiteIsolation/iframe/wheel-scrolls-an-isolated-iframe.html
+++ b/Tests/LibWeb/Text/input/SiteIsolation/iframe/wheel-scrolls-an-isolated-iframe.html
@@ -15,7 +15,10 @@
                 headers: { "Content-Type": "text/html" },
                 body: `<!DOCTYPE html><style>body { margin: 0; height: 3000px; }</style><script>
                     addEventListener("scroll", () => parent.postMessage({ scrolled: scrollY > 0 }, "*"));
-                    parent.postMessage("ready", "*");
+                    requestAnimationFrame(() => requestAnimationFrame(() => {
+                        internals.synchronizeCompositor();
+                        parent.postMessage("ready", "*");
+                    }));
                 <\/script>`,
             })
         );
